id: pm-vcs-tracker-admission
title: Admit coherent tracker pairs into native revisions
description: "Certify selected canonical item documents and history heads before native capture, including SDK-certifiable transaction membership."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#180"
created_at: "2026-11-04T21:41:27.622Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-05T02:44:19.988Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Concurrent writers yield a verified coherent snapshot or typed retry; custom folders and formats use SDK resolution; mismatched pairs never publish a native tip; resume checks only affected records; typed SDK plus CLI, compact TOON/JSON, strict bounded schemas, docs, seeded model and interleaving tests, public non-git real-data evidence."
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-04T21:41:38.414Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: core public SDK provides locateItem/readLocatedItem, readHistorySnapshot/verifyHistoryEntries, item transaction journals and canonical codecs. Core workspace/item transactions commit tracker changes but do not version arbitrary source and tracker artifacts together. pm-vcs checkpoints check assurance scope after capture; pm-evidence and pm-context consume evidence/context rather than admit native tips. This feature owns selected tracker capture admission only, without a distributed transaction or a new history codec. No duplicate item or upstream capture feature found."
  "2026-11-04T21:49:37.628Z",codex-agent,"Implemented SDK TrackerCapture plus vcs commit-tracker over one strict bounded selection schema. Capture retains SDK-verified exact bytes; native publication checks expected parent and modifies the latest index under the existing store lease. Retry sessions are explicitly process-local: only affected records are re-resolved, settings changes invalidate retained proofs, and successful sessions cannot publish twice. Committed SDK journal result membership is required for item-transaction markers; missing or partial evidence produces a payload-free retry coordinate. No status-name decisions, tracker mutations, distributed-transaction claim or durable replay journal were added."
  "2026-11-04T22:02:25.458Z",codex-agent,"Public committed tracker validation on a disposable non-git copy: 175 items, 175 histories, 3312 history entries, 350 native files, 7167088 selected bytes (5681588 history bytes), zero retries, 77860 ms measured; source tracker digest unchanged. Added selected-member transaction closure: if a committed SDK transaction appears in a later captured pair, previously captured selected members missing that transaction become affected retry records. This avoids mixing pre-transaction and post-transaction selected members while keeping resume narrow."
  "2026-11-04T22:11:39.777Z",codex-agent,"Validation: seeded model (seed 0x53295) passed 500 sequences across native bundle replay, signed change-bundle replay, file fetch/clone, older revisions, whitespace/CRLF, relationships, explicit scope under ambient focus and random custom status IDs/roles. All state comparisons use SDK read-back against revision-indexed SDK-produced model documents. Targeted admission tests passed 17/17; separate model passed 1/1 with 500 sequences. New capture module measured 100/100/100/100; CLI reader separately measured 100/100/100/100 after bounded-read control-flow cleanup. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings (606 declarations), and zero-duplication gate passed. Pinned SDK remains 2026.10.30; peer and manifest host floor now match the history snapshot and transaction certificate APIs instead of advertising older unsupported hosts."
  "2026-11-04T22:11:44.695Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in disposable source copies: disabling only the canonical SDK history-agreement guard fails the torn-pair regression 1/1; disabling only expected-native-tip CAS fails the competing-session regression 1/1. Original worktree functions were never mutated; restored passing torn-pair and CLI regression executed through pm test --run --progress (2/2 passed). Packed acceptance passed npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx and project-local layouts on one artifact; output sizes were JSON 130 bytes, TOON 107 bytes and retry 339 bytes. Final rebuilt artifact acceptance is being repeated after the host-floor metadata update. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates will run in CI; no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-11-04T22:12:55.350Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and documentation are ready for orchestrator review. Host compatibility now refuses pre-2026.10.30 runtimes through the existing manifest contract without changing the pinned development SDK. Real data, deterministic interleavings (including selected-member transaction closure), model replay, compact outputs and behavioral revert evidence are recorded above. Final-head CI will provide unchanged npm plus Bun release:check results; the PR will carry the exact run URL and counts. Release this agent claim for the verifier; keep the item in progress until the orchestrator verifies and closes it."
  "2026-11-04T22:18:55.153Z",codex-agent,"Final review preserved existing native executable modes, copied provenance and deterministic legacy FileId migration when replacing selected bytes; the added native-field regression passed 1/1. The complete admission plus manifest run passed 20/20, including 500 seeded sequences and transaction-read boundary competition. Scope failures now identify outside-workspace records with an actionable compact retry; terminal SDK refusals retain their stable code in CLI error text. Strict pm health passes using the CI-pinned project extension; the existing provenance-value advisory is retained without any history repair. The initial local extension-host skew matches existing pm-vcs-5lre and was resolved by reproducing the CI extension setup."
  "2026-11-04T22:24:39.646Z",codex-agent,"Final feature artifact SHA-256 a09e991c0574c95c13f0ec2e4564d37a32e448a2eeebdf0905a17c3bb3cd5c62 passed all five consumer layouts (npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx, project-local); JSON/TOON/retry receipts measured 130/107/339 bytes. Latest focused admission tests passed 18/18 with both new modules at 100 percent in every coverage dimension; seeded model passed 1/1 (500 sequences); manifest conformance passed 2/2; final edge/native-field checks passed 4/4. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings, duplicate gate, changelog generation/check and strict health pass. Implementation evidence is complete; full final-head npm/Bun release gates remain CI evidence to be linked in the PR. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item intentionally not closed."
  "2026-11-04T22:32:11.782Z",codex-agent,"Additional concurrency proof found a native HEAD identity gap: switching to another branch at the same revision satisfied a tip-only guard. The new non-git regression failed before the fix (1/1), then the capture was bound to its original branch or detached HEAD and publication rechecks both identity and tip inside the writer lease. Regression covers branch-to-branch and branch-to-detached switches plus valid detached publication. This follow-up supersedes the initial PR head; only the subsequent exact-head CI run is final gate evidence. Final packed-layout validation is repeated for the updated artifact."
  "2026-11-04T22:52:38.011Z",codex-agent,"Broader native-record probing exposed the same narrow-round-trip risk highlighted in the task: the existing codec rejected SDK-valid custom status IDs under recordPaths. Native record transport now keeps unknown status IDs opaque through the public SDK codec without assigning lifecycle roles, while admission supplies the canonical document read under the actual SDK workspace schema, including status aliases. The seeded 500-sequence model was rerun with configured native record storage and passed 1/1; existing record tests passed 12/12. A dedicated malformed-shape/custom-status/alias read-back regression verifies that the materialized SDK document and history still agree. Read-only sealed public data validation also passed 175/175 with 3312 history entries, 350 files, 7167088 selected bytes and unchanged source bytes (18860 ms). Final PR and CI evidence must use the next head; earlier runs are superseded."
  "2026-11-05T01:58:20.935Z",codex-agent,"Review round at c928475: fetched all nine unresolved threads and every comment (no further pages), plus latest CodeRabbit review body. No Outside diff range section; its follow-up root-precedence finding and materialization nit are included. Remote branch is current and contains origin/main (3 ahead, 0 behind). Verify findings, self-review capture invariants, record behavioral revert proofs, then run unchanged npm and Bun release gates. No thread replies/resolutions, merge or release."
  "2026-11-05T02:05:41.355Z",codex-agent,"Verified all nine findings as valid. Implementation now shares commit preflight, checks active view membership and duplicate indexed IDs under the writer lease, preserves payload derivation, limits receipt membership to prepared item-mutation outcomes, checks all required same-item markers, and distinguishes blob capture from unrepresentable native records. Working status and ordinary staging share SDK registry normalization; selection paths share sourceWorkingRoot. Added real non-git tracker regressions, allowed create/adopted-step cases, both refusal cases and artifact rebuild acceptance. Focused validation and disposable behavioral reverts follow."
  "2026-11-05T02:25:43.053Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert receipts: all nine unresolved findings and review follow-ups were verified in disposable source copies; only the corresponding changed function or behavior was reverted; the package worktree implementation was never mutated. schema hashing: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='record codecs' test/tracker-admission.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS. sparse view: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='captured new paths' test/tracker-admission.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS. derivation: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='captured replacements' test/tracker-admission.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS. commit refusals: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='captured commit refusals' test/tracker-admission.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS. missing receipt steps: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='receipt steps missing' test/tracker-admission.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS. membership filter: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='unrelated workspace' test/tracker-admission.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS. blob decoding: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='blob captures' test/tracker-admission.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS. duplicate path: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='moved tracker paths' test/tracker-admission.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS. fresh artifact: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='install validator' test/tracker-admission-artifact.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS. root precedence: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='relative selection' test/tracker-admission.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS. SDK audit suffix: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='create and adopted' test/tracker-admission.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS. materialization oracle: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='500 seeded' test/tracker-admission.test.ts; behavioral revert FAILED, restored PASS in the complete seeded run. Additional JSON-markdown codec proof: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=JSON-markdown test/tracker-admission.test.ts fails with released record codec functions restored, then passes with the fix. The strengthened materialization assertion rejects a corrupted materializer before any formatting overwrite (seed 0x53295)."
  "2026-11-05T02:25:44.471Z",codex-agent,"Self-review also fixed SDK create-marker audit suffixes and configured JSON-markdown record hashing/body round-trips, and scoped duplicate-path rejection to the selected tracker namespace (unrelated source documents with the same filename remain allowed). Plain non-git root trackers, deep blob metadata, custom registry aliases, legacy records, created items and adopted lifecycle steps have passing allow cases. Linked pm test --run --progress passed all 33 selected tests; the 500-sequence model also passed. Strict tracker health is clean except its retained provenance advisory; pinned merge install corrected shared merge-driver drift without changing history. Full unchanged npm and Bun release gates follow on a committed source/self-host snapshot."
  "2026-11-05T02:36:42.538Z",codex-agent,"Additional verified instances of the review defect classes: canonical commit preparation now validates signatures and item headers before captured index publication, using the same native encoder as ordinary commits. Exact regression: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"captured signature\" test/tracker-admission.test.ts; removing only the preflight encoding in a disposable copy FAILS the byte-identical index assertion, restored implementation PASSES (invalid signature and invalid item-header corpus). Strict unknown-field schemas also require their file-backed custom field definitions when hashing aliases. Exact regression: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"file-backed custom fields\" test/tracker-admission.test.ts; reverting only workingSchema field hydration FAILS unchanged-item status, restored implementation PASSES. Both were executed through linked pm test --run --progress (2/2 passed). The earlier full-gate attempt was stopped before completion to keep final evidence on one unchanged committed implementation; both full gates restart after the source/self-host refresh."
  "2026-11-05T02:44:16.579Z",codex-agent,"Commit refusal preflight is now pure for the object store as well as the index: buildTree uses one canonical algorithm for candidate hashing and actual publication, with a publish flag controlling only storage. A seeded property test (25 candidate trees) verifies identical IDs and unchanged candidate object inventory. Exact regression: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"captured signature\" test/tracker-admission.test.ts; reverting only candidate hashing to tree publication FAILS the new unchanged-object-inventory assertion; restored implementation PASSES. Linked pm acceptance also covers the seeded property and actual npm archives with stale and absent dist. Full release gates restart from the subsequent committed source and self-host snapshot."
